 music catalog through compilations and reissuances of previously released music and video titles, as well as previously unreleased materials. It also owns and acquires rights to approximately two million musical compositions comprising pop hits, American standards, folk songs, and motion picture and theatrical compositions, as well as administers the music and soundtracks of various third-party television and film producers and studios. In addition, the company conducts its operation primarily through a collection of record labels, such as Asylum, Big Beat, Canvasback, East West, Erato, FFRR, Nonesuch, Parlophone, Reprise, Sire, Spinnin' Records, and Warner Classics and Warner Records Nashville. Further, it markets, distributes, and sells music and video products to retailers and wholesale distributors; independent labels to retail and wholesale distributors; and various distribution centers and ventures, as well as retail outlets, online physical retailers, streaming services, and download services. Its catalog includes songwriters and composers; and various genres, including pop, rock, jazz, classical, country, R&B, hip-hop, rap, reggae, Latin, folk, alternative, blues, gospel, and other Christian music. The company was founded in 1929 and is headquartered in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Robert  Kyncl | President, CEO & Director | Age 54 | Compensation: $5.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 5K people. Revenue per employee of $1.2M ranks in the top quartile among Communication Services peers, improving at 7%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $98K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $10K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Warner Music Group Corp. is a large-cap communication services business with a $16.4B market cap on $6.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years and +9% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 16% against a 9% cost of capital, a 8-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $539M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 8 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.86\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 3.9\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 2.4% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 69% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.6879733523608376},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.8% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Communication Services ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"AI-generated content commoditisation \u2014 as creation costs collapse toward zero, content libraries lose pricing power and differentiation narrows.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Warner Music Group (WMG) Jumped, What Is Behind The Fresh Attention?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/media/nasdaq-wmg/warner-music-group/news/warner-music-group-wmg-jumped-what-is-behind-the-fresh-atten","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793871049.055,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.917,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Precision Trading with Warner Music Group Corp. (WMG) Risk Zones","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/134/Precision_Trading_with_Warner_Music_Group_Corp._WMG_Risk_Zones_110426093404_1793802844.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793802844.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Adobe Music Deal Might Change The Case For Investing In Warner Music Group Stock","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/media/nasdaq-wmg/warner-music-group/news/adobe-music-deal-might-change-the-case-for-investing-in-warn","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793960920.726,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.402,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"JPMorgan Chase Reveals 3.4% Stake in Warner Music Group in Latest SEC Filing","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/jpmorgan-chase-reveals-34-stake-in-warner-music-group-in-latest-sec-filing","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793896609.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"Can Warner Music Stock Get Back To Where It Was?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://fi